# Paths the `tauri dev` file watcher must NOT rebuild on.
#
# The watcher watches this whole crate directory, and the frontend lives inside it at
# src-frontend/. Without this, every .tsx edit — and every `npm test` run, because vitest writes
# node_modules/.vite/vitest/results.json — killed the running app and relaunched it, losing
# whatever project was open. In dev the frontend is served by Vite on devUrl and hot-reloads on
# its own, so the Rust side has no reason to rebuild for it.
#
# IMPORTANT: list the noisy SUBDIRECTORIES, never `src-frontend/` itself. These ignore rules also
# apply to the scan the Tauri CLI uses to locate the frontend directory, so hiding src-frontend/
# wholesale hides src-frontend/package.json too — the CLI then falls back to the repo root and
# `beforeDevCommand` dies with "Could not read package.json".
#
# `tauri build` is unaffected: it bundles frontendDist via beforeBuildCommand, not via this watcher.
src-frontend/src/
src-frontend/node_modules/
src-frontend/dist/
src-frontend/scripts/
